  "$comment": "The AndroidX Compose samples this repository vendors and publishes as ONE catalog, the `compose-ui-samples` system on preview.coo.ee: every `androidx.compose` sample tree with a Compose Multiplatform desktop artifact, EXCEPT material3, which yschimke/m3-catalog publishes as `m3-samples` beside the kit it is paired with. Excluded on purpose: material3 and its adaptive/window-size-class siblings (m3-catalog), `remote`, `runtime-livedata`/`-rxjava*`, `ui-viewbinding`, `ui-text-google-fonts` and `material-navigation` (Android-only, no desktop artifact), the `ui-test*` trees (test-rule samples, nothing to render), and `ui-tooling-preview` (its samples are empty `@PreviewWrapper` demos with no content to render). Every library shares ONE `ref` because the Compose core libraries release as a single train: androidx-main as of 2026-08-12, the day the 1.12.0 train was published — the same commit yschimke/m3-catalog measured as the exact @sample match for Compose Multiplatform 1.12 (see its ui-samples-catalog/import.json). `ref` is a COMMIT SHA, never a branch, so a render is reproducible and an upstream bump is a reviewable diff. `section` is the catalog tab each library's groups are published under. `androidSamples` is the artifact AndroidX publishes for the same sample tree; the Android lane (:catalog-android) depends on it at the androidx.dev snapshot build pinned in gradle/libs.versions.toml, and scripts/android-samples.mjs reads its sources jar to generate that lane's wrappers.",
